Z||000000||FieroMaster88||01-30-2001||01:11 AM||||Well, I have one week left before it is no Fiero!!!  I am going to have it at school so I can rebuild my trans.  I think I am the only person who can blow up the clutch on an automatic transmission.  And the really depressing part, the car only has 30K miles on it!  DOH!<P>Well, now the good part.  It is only going to cost me $300 to rebuild it totaly.  I am gettin the shift kit for the auto trans from the Fiero Store, a higher stall torque converter, a new exhaust system, and some ignition stuff.  I have to remove the whole engine cradle to get the trans out, so it makes it easier to do the upgrades.  Now if I could only find some cheap lowering springs for a 88 Fiero.........Right, cheap suspension components for a 88!!! LOL!  <P>Well, I am done crying for now.  If anyone has any good suggestions for a preformance exhaust system that will make a 4 cyl sound mean, let me know.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">   <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles<BR>84 Indy Fiero (restoration Project)||||reg||9
